{#
    Category against Shopware version.

    A real table, not a grid of divs. The data is a table, every cell has two headers,
    and a screen reader that knows it is a table can say "Payment, 6.7, 71 percent"
    without us inventing labels for that.

    The shade is a share, not a count. Payment holds sixty extensions and subscriptions
    holds one, so a count would draw the size of the category and nothing else, which
    is a fact already on the chart above this one.

    Five steps of one hue. Past five, neighbouring shades stop being rankable and the
    grid becomes decoration. Zero gets no shade at all, because none of a category is
    a different statement from the least of it, and the number is in every cell
    regardless so the colour is never carrying the value alone.
#}
<section class="panel chart chart--wide" id="chart-{{ chart.id }}">
    <h2>{{ chart.title }}</h2>
    <p class="chart-question">{{ chart.question }}</p>

    <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data heatmap">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Category</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="num">Total</th>
                    {% for version in chart.versions %}
                        <th scope="col" class="num">{{ version }}</th>
                    {% endfor %}
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in chart.rows %}
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row">{{ row.label }}</th>
                        <td class="num muted">{{ row.total }}</td>
                        {% for cell in row.cells %}
                            <td class="num heat step-{{ cell.step }}"
                                title="{{ cell.value }} of {{ row.total }} declare support for {{ cell.version }}">{{ cell.percent }}%</td>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <p class="board-rule"><span class="board-rule-label">Rule</span> {{ chart.rule }}</p>
</section>
